From 29eeef1c5fd7699dc6e71c49aa305ab895a62b2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 23:34:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06836/11362] ARC round-2 (codex): lp85 FULL CLEAR (L8) +
 ka59/tu93 +1 each

Continuation of the same-day breadth-campaign game loop. lp85 reaches its
terminal level: L7 -> L8, frame reports state=WIN and win_levels=8, no
further level exists. tu93 -- a game with a documented prior honest null
(v19: "richest adversary dossier of the session... genuine two-lock wall")
-- broke through this round: it was a charger-ordering dependency puzzle,
not a dead end, confirming v19's own "enter from above pre-fires the
charger harmlessly" hypothesis was the right unlock direction. ka59 solved
L5 (confirming a prior scouting pass's mod-3 phase-readout hypothesis) and
made partial L6 progress (stuck in an isolated one-way chamber, not banked).

Fixed a resolver bug found while verifying tu93: its artifact stores labels
as bare ints, but the GameAdapter's apply() expects a JSON-object string
({"action": N}) -- added the missing serialization step (same bug class as
several fixes earlier this session).

Every claimed win independently re-verified per project discipline (5x
fresh env.reset() + replay via the correct GameAdapter) before being
recorded. reproducible_total_levels: 128 -> 131 (verified against a fresh
sum). 12 of 18 round-2 games now processed; remaining: lf52, r11l, re86,
s5i5, su15.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
